ei f\u00fcr Menschen mit Verst\u00e4ndnisschwierigkeiten","Barrierefrei","Anpassungen f\u00fcr blinde und sehbehinderte Menschen","Anpassungen f\u00fcr geh\u00f6rlose und h\u00f6rgesch\u00e4digte Menschen.","Barrierefrei f\u00fcr Fu\u00dfg\u00e4nger mit Gehhilfe","Barrierefreies WC"],"it":["Accessibile alle persone con difficolt\u00e0 di comprensione","Accessibile","Disposizioni per persone non vedenti e ipovedenti","Disposizioni per persone non udenti e ipoudenti","Accessibile ai pedoni con supporti","WC idoneo"],"sp":["Habilitado para personas con dificultades de comprensi\u00f3n","Habilitado","Equipos para personas con problemas de visi\u00f3n y audici\u00f3n","Equipos para personas sordas y con problemas de audici\u00f3n","Habilitado para peatones con aud\u00edfonos","Ba\u00f1os adaptados"],"pt":[null,null,null,null,null,null],"cn":[null,null,null,null,null,null]}},"facebook_link":null,"publication_state":"public","last_updated_at":"2023-03-26T04:05:20+02:00","published_at":"2021-09-14T10:33:03+02:00","backoffice_id":239024,"import_origin":null,"sub_type":"expo","show_in_agenda":true,"ranking":0.19374586123029},{"id":546226,"date_start":"2022-11-26","date_end":"2023-09-03","date_next":"2023-03-26","accept_article27":true,"accept_cultuurbon":false,"accept_paspartoe":false,"is_closed_on_public_holidays":false,"is_closed_on_school_holidays":false,"is_only_by_appointment":false,"is_permanent":false,"is_free":false,"is_online":false,"is_canceled":false,"is_soldout":false,"categories":{"main":{"id":23,"translations":{"fr":"Exposition","nl":"Tentoonstellingen","en":"Exhibition","de":"Ausstellung","it":"Esposizioni","sp":"Exhibici\u00f3n","pt":null,"cn":null}},"others":{"list":[36,42],"translations":{"fr":["Mus\u00e9es et art centers","Peinture"],"nl":["Musea en kunstcentra","Schilderkunst"],"en":["Museums and art centers","Painting"],"de":["Museen & Kunstzentren","Malerei"],"it":["Musei e centri artistici","Pittura"],"sp":["Museos y centros de arte","Pintura"],"pt":[null,null],"cn":[null,null]}}},"languages":{"spoken":["fr","nl","en"],"subtitles":[]},"translations":{"fr":{"name":"Ren\u00e9e Demeester, paysages abstraits","shortdescr":"Le mus\u00e9e consacre un hommage \u00e0 Ren\u00e9e Demeester (1927-2022), une artiste belge abstraite r\u00e9cemment disparue.  Figure remarquable de l\u2019Abstraction belge des ann\u00e9es 1960\/80, elle sut d\u00e9velopper son propre style et le faire \u00e9voluer.","longdescr":"L'exposition intitul\u00e9e 'Paysages abstraits' rassemble des toiles abstraites inspir\u00e9es des lieux qui lui \u00e9taient chers : de la nature luxuriante du Katanga aux prairies cl\u00f4tur\u00e9es du Pajottenland, des espaces construits de Bruxelles aux horizons ouverts de la mer du Nord. Elle donne l\u2019occasion au public de se familiariser avec cette artiste tout aussi talentueuse que discr\u00e8te. A d\u00e9couvrir \u00e0 partir du 26 novembre!\r\n\r\n\u201cTout est en m\u00eame temps lointain et proche. Tout bouge, et tout est au point fixe. Ce n\u2019est pas un paradoxe, c\u2019est le myst\u00e8re avec lequel il faut faire bon m\u00e9nage.\u201d\r\n\r\nRen\u00e9e Demeester, 1973","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.magrittemuseum.be\/index.php\/fr\/visite\/expositions-temporaires-2\/expo-renee-demeester\/","email":"info@magrittemuseum.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":"+32 2 428 26 26","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/fr\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.546226"},"nl":{"name":"Ren\u00e9e Demeester, abstracte landschappen","shortdescr":"Het museum wijdt een solotentoonstelling aan Ren\u00e9e Demeester, die in april 2022 van ons is heengegaan. Binnen de Belgische abstracte kunst van de jaren 1960\u20131980 was ze immers een opmerkelijke figuur: een harde werkster met een eigen stijl en met een vormentaal die constant verder evolueerde.","longdescr":"De expo \u201cAbstracte landschappen\u201d brengt abstracte schilderijen die ge\u00efnspireerd zijn op de plaatsen die haar dierbaar waren: van de weelderige natuur van Katanga tot de ingesloten weiden van het Pajottenland, van de bebouwde ruimte van Brussel tot de open horizon van de Noordzee. Ze biedt de ideale gelegenheid om deze getalenteerde en discrete kunstenares beter te leren kennen. Te ontdekken vanaf 26 november!\r\n\r\n\u201cAlles is ver weg en tegelijk dichtbij. Alles beweegt, en alles is immobiel. Dit is geen paradox, het is het mysterie waarmee we moeten leven.\u201d\r\n\r\nRen\u00e9e Demeester, 1973","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.magrittemuseum.be\/index.php\/nl\/bezoek\/tijdelijke-tentoonstellingen\/expo-renee-demeester\/","email":"info@magrittemuseum.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":"+32 2 428 26 26","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/nl\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.546226"},"en":{"name":"Ren\u00e9e Demeester, abstract landscapes","shortdescr":"The museum is devoting an exhibition to Ren\u00e9e Demeester (1927-2022), a Belgian abstract artist who passed away recently.  She was an outstanding figure of Belgian abstraction in the 1960s and 1980s, and was able to develop her own style and make it evolve.","longdescr":"The exhibition entitled 'Abstract Landscapes' brings together abstract paintings inspired by the places that were dear to her: from the lush nature of Katanga to the enclosed meadows of Pajottenland, from the built-up spaces of Brussels to the open horizons of the North Sea. It gives the public the opportunity to get to know this talented and discreet artist. To be discovered from 26 November!\r\n\r\n\u201cEverything is distant and close at the same time. Everything moves, and everything is at a fixed point. This is not a paradox, it is the mystery that must be dealt with.\u201d\r\n\r\nRen\u00e9e Demeester, 1973","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.magrittemuseum.be\/index.php\/en\/visit\/temporary-exhibitions-2\/exhibition-renee-demeester\/","email":"info@magrittemuseum.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":"+32 2 428 26 26","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/en\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.546226"},"de":{"name":"Ren\u00e9e Demeester, paysages abstraits","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.magrittemuseum.be\/index.php\/fr\/visite\/expositions-temporaires-2\/expo-renee-demeester\/","email":"info@magrittemuseum.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":"+32 2 428 26 26","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/de\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.546226"},"it":{"name":"Ren\u00e9e Demeester, paysages abstraits","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.magrittemuseum.be\/index.php\/fr\/visite\/expositions-temporaires-2\/expo-renee-demeester\/","email":"info@magrittemuseum.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":"+32 2 428 26 26","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/it\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.546226"},"sp":{"name":"Ren\u00e9e Demeester, paysages abstraits","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.magrittemuseum.be\/index.php\/fr\/visite\/expositions-temporaires-2\/expo-renee-demeester\/","email":"info@magrittemuseum.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":"+32 2 428 26 26","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/sp\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.546226"},"pt":{"name":"Ren\u00e9e Demeester, paysages abstraits","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.magrittemuseum.be\/index.php\/fr\/visite\/expositions-temporaires-2\/expo-renee-demeester\/","email":"info@magrittemuseum.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":"+32 2 428 26 26","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/pt\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.546226"},"cn":{"name":"Ren\u00e9e Demeester, paysages abstraits","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.magrittemuseum.be\/index.php\/fr\/visite\/expositions-temporaires-2\/expo-renee-demeester\/","email":"info@magrittemuseum.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":"+32 2 428 26 26","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/cn\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.546226"}},"place":{"id":233245,"translations":{"fr":{"name":"Mus\u00e9e-Ren\u00e9 Magritte (Maison)","address_street_name":"Rue Esseghem","address_street_number":"135","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@magrittemuseum.be","website":"http:\/\/www.magrittemuseum.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 428 26 26","phone_booking":"+32 2 428 26 26","address_zip":"1090","address_city":"Jette","address_line1":"Rue Esseghem, 135","address_line2":"1090 Jette","description_web":"Le Mus\u00e9e Ren\u00e9 Magritte est situ\u00e9 dans la maison o\u00f9 le c\u00e9l\u00e8bre peintre surr\u00e9aliste v\u00e9cut et travailla pendant vingt-quatre ans (1930-1954). Magritte loue le rez-de-chauss\u00e9e avec jardin . En 1932, il construit \u00e0 l\u2019arri\u00e8re de celui-ci le Studio Dongo o\u00f9 il r\u00e9alise des projets de publicit\u00e9. C\u2019est dans la salle \u00e0 manger-atelier qu\u2019il peint le plus souvent et qu\u2019il r\u00e9alise pr\u00e8s de la moiti\u00e9 de ses oeuvres.\r\nAu 135 de la rue Esseghem est aussi \u00e9tabli le quartier g\u00e9n\u00e9ral des surr\u00e9alistes belges. Ils s\u2019y r\u00e9unissent chaque semaine et y organisent toutes sortes de tableaux vivants. \r\n\r\nDepuis novembre 2019, un nouveau mus\u00e9e sur l'Art abstrait est ouvert dans le b\u00e2timent voisin et lui est reli\u00e9 www.abstractartmuseum.be\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":"https:\/\/ticket.visit.brussels\/fr\/233245\/musee-rene-magritte-maison\/shop","sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"nl":{"name":"Ren\u00e9 Magritte Museum (Huis)","address_street_name":"Esseghemstraat","address_street_number":"135","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@magrittemuseum.be","website":"http:\/\/www.magrittemuseum.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 428 26 26","phone_booking":"+32 2 428 26 26","address_zip":"1090","address_city":"Jette","address_line1":"Esseghemstraat, 135","address_line2":"1090 Jette","description_web":"Het Ren\u00e9 Magritte Museum is gevestigd in het huis waar de beroemde, surrealistische kunstenaar 24 jaar gewoond en gewerkt heeft (1930-\u201854). Magritte betrok er het gelijkvloers, had er een tuin en bouwde in 1932 achter in die tuin Studio Dongo, waar hij ontwerpen voor publiciteit realiseerde. In de eetkamer tevens atelier schilderde hij meestal. Op deze plek zou hij vrijwel de helft van al zijn schilderijen en gouaches realiseren. \r\nIn de Esseghemstraat 135 was ook het hoofdkwartier van de Belgische surrealisten gevestigd, ze vergaderden er op zaterdagavond en organiseerden er allerlei tableaux vivants. \r\n\r\nSinds november 2019 wordt hiernaast een museum voor abstracte kunst geopend. Beide musea zijn verbonden met een tussendeur www.abstractartmuseum.be\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":"https:\/\/ticket.visit.brussels\/nl\/233245\/musee-rene-magritte-maison\/shop","sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"en":{"name":"Ren\u00e9 Magritte Museum (house)","address_street_name":"Rue Esseghem","address_street_number":"135","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@magrittemuseum.be","website":"http:\/\/www.magrittemuseum.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 428 26 26","phone_booking":"+32 2 428 26 26","address_zip":"1090","address_city":"Jette","address_line1":"Rue Esseghem, 135","address_line2":"1090 Jette","description_web":"The Ren\u00e9 Magritte Museum is situated in the house where the famous, surrealist artist lived and worked for 24 years (1930-54). Magritte lived on the ground floor and built in the back of the garden Studio Dongo, where he executed designs for publicity work. He painted most of the time in the living room annex atelier. In that room he would produce more or less half the amount of his paintings and gouaches. \r\nThe headquarters of the Belgian Surrealists was also in the Esseghemstraat 135, where they held their meetings on Saturday evenings and where they organized several tableaux vivants.\r\n\r\nSince November 2019, a new museum of abstract art has opened next door. Both museums are connected with each other www.abstractartmuseum.be \r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":"https:\/\/ticket.visit.brussels\/en\/233245\/musee-rene-magritte-maison\/shop","sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"de":{"name":"Ren\u00e9 Magritte Museum \u2013 Museum f\u00fcr abstrakte Kunst","address_street_name":"Rue Esseghem","address_street_number":"135","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@magrittemuseum.be","website":"http:\/\/www.magrittemuseum.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 428 26 26","phone_booking":"+32 2 428 26 26","address_zip":"1090","address_city":"Jette","address_line1":"Rue Esseghem, 135","address_line2":"1090 Jette","description_web":"Das Ren\u00e9 Magritte Museum ist in doppeltes Museum, das sich sowohl dem Surrealismus als auch der abstrakten Kunst aus Belgien widmet. Mit dieser Initiative soll daran erinnert werden, dass Magritte - bevor er sich 1926 dem Surrealismus zuwandte - auch ein Pionier auf dem Gebiet der abstrakten Kunst war. Das Museum erstreckt sich \u00fcber zwei H\u00e4user. ","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"it":{"name":"Maison-Mus\u00e9e Ren\u00e9 Magritte","address_street_name":"Rue Esseghem","address_street_number":"135","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@magrittemuseum.be","website":"http:\/\/www.magrittemuseum.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 428 26 26","phone_booking":"+32 2 428 26 26","address_zip":"1090","address_city":"Jette","address_line1":"Rue Esseghem, 135","address_line2":"1090 Jette","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"sp":{"name":"La Casa-Museo Ren\u00e9 Magritte","address_street_name":"Rue Esseghem","address_street_number":"135","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@magrittemuseum.be","website":"http:\/\/www.magrittemuseum.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 428 26 26","phone_booking":"+32 2 428 26 26","address_zip":"1090","address_city":"Jette","address_line1":"Rue Esseghem, 135","address_line2":"1090 Jette","description_web":"El Museo Ren\u00e9 Magritte se encuentra en la casa donde el famoso pintor surrealista vivi\u00f3 durante veinticuatro a\u00f1os. Este espacio vital, recreado con los muebles originales, inspir\u00f3 la obra de Magritte. En el comedor de este apartamento de alquiler, el artista pint\u00f3 casi la mitad de su obra. Este discreto lugar presenci\u00f3 su per\u00edodo m\u00e1s creativo, que dio como resultado lienzos grandiosos. El 135 de la calle Esseghem tambi\u00e9n era el cuartel general de los surrealistas belgas. Los amigos del pintor se reun\u00edan all\u00ed todas las semanas y organizaban todo tipo de eventos. Muchas actividades subversivas, libros, revistas y panfletos nacieron de estos encuentros. Estas actividades se ilustran claramente en las dos plantas superiores del museo a trav\u00e9s de obras originales, fotos, objetos, cartas y documentos personales. Esta casa se restaur\u00f3 y transform\u00f3 en museo entre 1993 y 1999. Est\u00e1 dise\u00f1ada para ser un homenaje permanente a uno de los pintores m\u00e1s brillantes de todos los tiempos. ","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"pt":{"name":"Casa-Museu Ren\u00e9 Magritte","address_street_name":"Rue Esseghem","address_street_number":"135","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@magrittemuseum.be","website":"http:\/\/www.magrittemuseum.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 428 26 26","phone_booking":"+32 2 428 26 26","address_zip":"1090","address_city":"Jette","address_line1":"Rue Esseghem, 135","address_line2":"1090 Jette","description_web":"Num bairro calmo dos arredores de Bruxelas, o Museu Magritte ocupa uma casa burguesa pequena e comum, onde o exponente m\u00e1ximo do movimento surrealista belga viveu, entre 1930 e 1954.","description_print":"","boo