ke und Bibliotheken mit knapp 40.000 Werken und Zeitschriften zu den Themen Architektur, St\u00e4dteplanung, Stadtgeschichte, Landschaften, G\u00e4rten und urbane \u00d6kosysteme.\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"it":{"name":"CIVA","address_street_name":"Rue de l'Ermitage","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@civa.brussels","website":"http:\/\/www.civa.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 642 24 50","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue de l'Ermitage","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"sp":{"name":"CIVA","address_street_name":"Rue de l'Ermitage","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@civa.brussels","website":"http:\/\/www.civa.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 642 24 50","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue de l'Ermitage","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":"Creado en 2016 por iniciativa de la Regi\u00f3n Bruselas-Capital, el CIVA re\u00fane una \u00fanica estructura de recursos, conocimiento y aprendizaje de varias asociaciones culturales activas en Bruselas en los campos de la arquitectura, urbanismo, paisajes y el estudio de ecosistemas: los Archivos de Arquitectura Moderna, la Biblioteca Ren\u00e9 Pech\u00e8re, los Fondos para la arquitectura, el Centro Paul Duvigneaud y el CIVA asbl, ahora disuelto.\r\nA trav\u00e9s de este proyecto cultural, la Fundaci\u00f3n CIVA contribuye al desarrollo del paisaje arquitect\u00f3nico y la cultura urbana como base para afrontar desaf\u00edos contempor\u00e1neos, poniendo especial \u00e9nfasis en Bruselas.\r\nSiempre tiene \u00e9xito a la hora de cumplir sus objetivos y tratar con un p\u00fablico amplio (adultos y ni\u00f1os, estudiantes, investigadores, arquitectos, paisajistas, amantes de la naturaleza, pol\u00edticos, etc), la fundaci\u00f3n CIVA organiza numerosos eventos y actividades en diferentes lugares, incluyendo exhibiciones permanentes y temporales, conferencias, debates y actividades educativas. Tambi\u00e9n dispone archivos excepcionales abiertos para todos los p\u00fablicos (documentos de arquitectos y paisajistas: planos, bocetos, modelos, muebles, etc.) y librer\u00edas que contienen casi 40.000 obras y peri\u00f3dicos de arquitectura, urbanismo, la historia de los pueblos y ciudades, paisajes, jardines y ecolog\u00eda urbana.\r\nEstas actividades y materiales est\u00e1n dise\u00f1ados para despertar la curiosidad y el inter\u00e9s de todo nuestro entorno, ya sea un hecho hist\u00f3rico o una construcci\u00f3n.\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"pt":{"name":"CIVA","address_street_name":"Rue de l'Ermitage","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@civa.brussels","website":"http:\/\/www.civa.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 642 24 50","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue de l'Ermitage","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"cn":{"name":"CIVA","address_street_name":"Rue de l'Ermitage","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@civa.brussels","website":"http:\/\/www.civa.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 642 24 50","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue de l'Ermitage","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null}},"neca":"art_center","facebook_id":null,"backoffice_id":1436,"location":{"lat":50.82873218,"lon":4.36569034},"region":"brussels","last_updated_at":"2023-03-15T17:35:05+01:00","published_at":"2013-10-19T01:14:20+02:00","import_origin":null,"external_id":null,"is_in_address_book":true,"is_in_vb_export":true,"resto_ranking":0},"media":[{"type":"photo","link":"https:\/\/agendabrussels.imgix.net\/96da16b0dcb2e0234714663a838c62b2360061f1.jpg","width":1160,"height":651,"ratio":1.78,"translations":{"fr":{"title":"Visites guid\u00e9es - Style Congo","copyright":"\u00a9 Objects That Are Dear to Him: Lessons on Building Colonial Houses in Congo, 2023"},"nl":{"title":"Visites guid\u00e9es - Style Congo","copyright":"\u00a9 Objects That Are Dear to Him: Lessons on Building Colonial Houses in Congo, 2023"},"en":{"title":"Visites guid\u00e9es - Style Congo","copyright":"\u00a9 Objects That Are Dear to Him: Lessons on Building Colonial Houses in Congo, 2023"},"de":{"title":"Visites guid\u00e9es - Style Congo","copyright":"\u00a9 Objects That Are Dear to Him: Lessons on Building Colonial Houses in Congo, 2023"},"it":{"title":"Visites guid\u00e9es - Style Congo","copyright":"\u00a9 Objects That Are Dear to Him: Lessons on Building Colonial Houses in Congo, 2023"},"sp":{"title":"Visites guid\u00e9es - Style Congo","copyright":"\u00a9 Objects That Are Dear to Him: Lessons on Building Colonial Houses in Congo, 2023"},"pt":{"title":"Visites guid\u00e9es - Style Congo","copyright":"\u00a9 Objects That Are Dear to Him: Lessons on Building Colonial Houses in Congo, 2023"},"cn":{"title":"Visites guid\u00e9es - Style Congo","copyright":"\u00a9 Objects That Are Dear to Him: Lessons on Building Colonial Houses in Congo, 2023"}}}],"dates":[{"day":"2023-03-30","doors":null,"start":"18:00:00","end":"19:30:00","is_soldout":false,"is_canceled":false},{"day":"2023-04-06","doors":null,"start":"18:00:00","end":"19:30:00","is_soldout":false,"is_canceled":false},{"day":"2023-04-22","doors":null,"start":"14:00:00","end":"15:30:00","is_soldout":false,"is_canceled":false},{"day":"2023-05-11","doors":null,"start":"18:00:00","end":"19:30:00","is_soldout":false,"is_canceled":false},{"day":"2023-06-01","doors":null,"start":"18:00:00","end":"19:30:00","is_soldout":false,"is_canceled":false},{"day":"2023-06-17","doors":null,"start":"14:00:00","end":"15:30:00","is_soldout":false,"is_canceled":false}],"prices":[{"translations":{"fr":{"name":"Normal"},"nl":{"name":"Normaal"},"en":{"name":"Normal"},"de":{"name":"Normal"},"it":{"name":"Normale"},"sp":{"name":"Normal"},"pt":{"name":"Normal"},"cn":{"name":"Normal"}},"value":12}],"child_events":[],"parent_events":[],"targets":{"list":[],"translations":{}},"tags":["annee_art_nouveau"],"is_part_of":"Ann\u00e9e Art Nouveau","accessibilities":{"list":[255,256,257,263,265],"translations":{"fr":["Accessible","Am\u00e9nagements pour les personnes aveugles et malvoyantes","Am\u00e9nagements pour personnes sourdes et malentendantes","Accessible aux pi\u00e9tons appareill\u00e9s","WC adapt\u00e9"],"nl":["Toegankelijk","Voorzieningen voor blinde en slechtziende personen","Voorzieningen voor dove en slechthorende personen","Toegankelijk voor voetgangers met hulpmiddelen","Aangepast toilet"],"en":["Accessible","Facilities for blind and partially-sighted persons","Facilities for deaf and hearing-impaired people","Accessible to pedestrians with mobility aids","Adapted toilet"],"de":["Barrierefrei","Anpassungen f\u00fcr blinde und sehbehinderte Menschen","Anpassungen f\u00fcr geh\u00f6rlose und h\u00f6rgesch\u00e4digte Menschen.","Barrierefrei f\u00fcr Fu\u00dfg\u00e4nger mit Gehhilfe","Barrierefreies WC"],"it":["Accessibile","Disposizioni per persone non vedenti e ipovedenti","Disposizioni per persone non udenti e ipoudenti","Accessibile ai pedoni con supporti","WC idoneo"],"sp":["Habilitado","Equipos para personas con problemas de visi\u00f3n y audici\u00f3n","Equipos para personas sordas y con problemas de audici\u00f3n","Habilitado para peatones con aud\u00edfonos","Ba\u00f1os adaptados"],"pt":[null,null,null,null,null],"cn":[null,null,null,null,null]}},"facebook_link":null,"publication_state":"public","last_updated_at":"2023-03-15T17:35:05+01:00","published_at":"2023-03-15T17:14:11+01:00","backoffice_id":273505,"import_origin":null,"sub_type":"tour","show_in_agenda":true,"ranking":0.29240177382129},{"id":551153,"date_start":"2023-03-12","date_end":"2023-04-29","date_next":"2023-03-30","accept_article27":false,"accept_cultuurbon":false,"accept_paspartoe":false,"is_closed_on_public_holidays":true,"is_closed_on_school_holidays":false,"is_only_by_appointment":false,"is_permanent":false,"is_free":true,"is_online":false,"is_canceled":false,"is_soldout":false,"categories":{"main":{"id":23,"translations":{"fr":"Exposition","nl":"Tentoonstellingen","en":"Exhibition","de":"Ausstellung","it":"Esposizioni","sp":"Exhibici\u00f3n","pt":null,"cn":null}},"others":{"list":[24,30],"translations":{"fr":["Galeries d'art","Peinture"],"nl":["Galeries","Schilderkunst"],"en":["Art Galleries","Painting"],"de":["Kunstgalerien","Malerei"],"it":["Gallerie d'arte","Pittura"],"sp":["Galer\u00edas de arte","Pintura"],"pt":[null,null],"cn":[null,null]}}},"languages":{"spoken":["fr","nl","en"],"subtitles":[]},"translations":{"fr":{"name":"Michiko Van de Velde - Timing","shortdescr":"Dans un certain nombre d'\u0153uvres, l'artiste s'int\u00e9resse \u00e0 la simultan\u00e9it\u00e9 de la lumi\u00e8re de Tokyo et de Bruxelles. En g\u00e9n\u00e9ral, cela varie beaucoup, n\u00e9anmoins deux fois par an, le lever du soleil \u00e0 Bruxelles et le coucher du soleil \u00e0 Tokyo co\u00efncident \u00e9tonnamment.\r\nSes autres travaux gravitent souvent autour de la \"capture de la lumi\u00e8re\" et du moment o\u00f9 une observation dispara\u00eet en un clin d'\u0153il.","longdescr":"\u201cComment parle-t-on de la lumi\u00e8re (au Japon)?\u201d\r\n\u201cQuelle lumi\u00e8re? Celle de quand?\u201d\r\n(extrait du Livre, \u00ab\u00a0Lumi\u00e8res \u5149\u00a0\u00bb, auto-\u00e9dition, 2017)\r\nLumi\u00e8re?\u00a0\r\nEspace?\u00a0\r\nTemps?\u00a0\u00a0\r\n\r\nDe quoi parlons-nous lorsque nous regardons le travail de Michiko Van de Velde ?\r\nEt dans quelle langue devons-nous parler ?\u00a0\r\nEn 2017, l\u2019artiste a cr\u00e9\u00e9 Lumi\u00e8res, un recueil de po\u00e9sie dans lequel elle a rassembl\u00e9 des dizaines de mots japonais qui nomment les diff\u00e9rentes nuances de la lumi\u00e8re, tels que :\r\n\u2028\u63a1\u5149[saik\u014d] Faire rentrer la lumi\u00e8re du dehors dans la maison,\u00a0\r\n\u8584\u65e5[usubi] Lumi\u00e8re faible, sourde, comme un ciel de Bruxelles, un voile gris.\u00a0\r\n\u4e5d\u5341\u6625\u5149\u00a0[kujun\u014d\u00a0shunk\u014d] Lumi\u00e8re paisible du printemps, qui dure 90 jours, de mars \u00e0 juin.\r\n\u6708\u767d[tsuki shiro] Quand la lune se l\u00e8ve, le ciel \u00e0 l'Est para\u00eet plus clair et plus blanc.\r\n\u6728\u6f0f\u308c\u65e5[komorebi] Le soleil filtre \u00e0 travers les arbres : jeu de la lumi\u00e8re dans les feuillages.\r\n\r\n\u00c0 la fin de cette petite ph\u00e9nom\u00e9nologie de la lumi\u00e8re, elle a ajout\u00e9 un autre mot japonais suivant\u00a0\u9593 [ma]. Ma est \u00e0 la fois espace et temps. Il signifie essentiellement un intervalle, une distance ou une p\u00e9riode de temps. En d'autres termes, une relation.  Fille d'une m\u00e8re japonaise et d'un p\u00e8re belge, Michiko incarne pour ainsi dire\u9593\u00a0[ma]. Elle vit \"entre\" deux cultures, entre deux espaces et deux temps.\r\n\r\nSans vouloir faire de psychologie, il semble que Michiko veuille saisir en images cette conscience de la pluralit\u00e9 du temps et de l'espace, et surtout du caract\u00e8re impalpable du temps.\u00a0\r\nC\u2019est dans ce changement permanent de la lumi\u00e8re que la fugacit\u00e9 du temps et de l\u2019espace deviennent pour elle \u00e0 la fois visibles et tangibles.\r\n\r\nDans un certain nombre d'\u0153uvres, Michiko Van de Velde s'int\u00e9resse \u00e0 la simultan\u00e9it\u00e9 de la lumi\u00e8re de Tokyo et de Bruxelles. En g\u00e9n\u00e9ral, cela varie beaucoup, n\u00e9anmoins deux fois par an, le lever du soleil \u00e0 Bruxelles et le coucher du soleil \u00e0 Tokyo co\u00efncident \u00e9tonnamment.\r\nSes autres travaux gravitent souvent autour de la \"capture de la lumi\u00e8re\" et du moment o\u00f9 une observation dispara\u00eet en un clin d'\u0153il.\r\n\r\nMichiko Van de Velde utilise une vari\u00e9t\u00e9 de techniques.\u00a0\r\nElle dessine ce qu\u2019elle voit ; des points lumineux qu\u2019elle marque au crayon sur le papier ou grave directement sur les plaques en m\u00e9tal.\r\n\r\nIn situ, elle dessine, peint ou \"disperse\" des paillettes de mica naturelles et r\u00e9fl\u00e9chissantes pour \"capter\" la lumi\u00e8re solaire incidente.\u00a0\r\nDepuis des trains en mouvement, elle peint des vues photographi\u00e9es en consid\u00e9rant le jeu des reflets de la lumi\u00e8re et les effets miroirs des fen\u00eatres dans les fen\u00eatres.\u00a0\r\n\r\nPar le biais de la vid\u00e9o, elle a captur\u00e9 la lumi\u00e8re color\u00e9e et vacillante des panneaux publicitaires qui irradie des voiles de brouillard dans la rue. Mais elle s'est aussi \" document\u00e9e \", notamment lorsqu'elle a essay\u00e9 de dessiner \u00e0 main lev\u00e9e des taches de lumi\u00e8re rondes qui tombaient \u00e0 travers le feuillage d'un arbre (\u6728\u6f0f\u308c\u65e5[komorebi]). En raison de la rotation de la terre, on remarque dans la vid\u00e9o, la vitesse \u00e0 laquelle ces points lumineux se d\u00e9placent rapidement sur la feuille blanche. Il est presque impossible de dessiner la tache dans son enti\u00e8ret\u00e9 car entre le d\u00e9but et la fin de son dessin, l\u2019ombre s'est d\u00e9j\u00e0 d\u00e9plac\u00e9e.\r\n\r\nCette lumi\u00e8re \" fugace \" et la volatilit\u00e9 des choses se retrouvent dans le mot\u00a0\u6728\u6f0f\u308c\u65e5[komorebi] o\u00f9 le kanji\u00a0\u6f0f[mo] inclut la r\u00e9f\u00e9rence \u00e0 une fuite et \u00e0 un vol.\u00a0\r\n\r\nNous devrions peut-\u00eatre consid\u00e9rer le travail de Michiko Van de Velde comme une r\u00e9\u00e9dition de \u2018Kunst der Fuge\u2019. Car, comme dans les fugues de J.S. Bach, elle transforme la volatilit\u00e9 et le caract\u00e8re insaisissable du temps en art de vivre.\r\n\r\nKoen Van Synghel, critique d'art","performers":"Michiko Van de Velde (\u00b01994, Brasschaat (B)), artiste Belgo-Japonaise, vit et travaille \u00e0 Bruxelles.","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.micheleschoonjansgallery.be","email":"info@micheleschoonjansgallery.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":"+32 478 71 62 96","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/fr\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.551153"},"nl":{"name":"Michiko Van de Velde - Timing","shortdescr":"In een aantal werken legt ze zich toe op de simultane\u00efteit van het licht in Tokyo en Brussel. Doorgaans is dat heel verschillend, maar twee keer per jaar, valt de zonsopgang in Brussel en de zonsondergang in Tokyo verrassend samen.\r\nIn haar ander werk draait het vaak om het \u2018vangen van het licht\u2019 en het ogenblik waarin een waarneming in een flits weer is verdwenen.","longdescr":"\u201cComment parle-t-on de la lumi\u00e8re (au Japon)?\u201d\r\n\u201cQuelle lumi\u00e8re? Celle de quand?\u201d\r\n(uit \u201c\u00a0Lumi\u00e8res\u5149 \u201d, auto-\u00e9dition, 2017)\r\nLicht?\u00a0\r\nRuimte?\u00a0\r\nTijd?\u00a0\u00a0\r\n\r\nOver wat spreken we, wanneer we naar het werk van\u00a0Michiko\u00a0Van de Velde kijken?\r\nEn in welke taal moeten we spreken?\u00a0\r\nIn 2017 maakte ze met Lumi\u00e8res een boekwerkje waarin ze tientallen Japanse woorden verzamelde die verschillende hoedanigheden van licht benoemen, zoals:\r\n\r\n\u63a1\u5149[saik\u014d] Het buitenlicht binnenlaten in huis,\u00a0\r\n\u8584\u65e5[usubi] zacht,dof licht, zoals een Brusselse lucht, een grijze sluier.\u00a0\r\n\u4e5d\u5341\u6625\u5149\u00a0[kujun\u014d\u00a0shunk\u014d] Rustig lentelicht, 90 dagen lang tussen maart en juni.\r\n\u6708\u767d[tsuki shiro] bij opkomende maan, lijkt de lucht in het Oosten helderder en witter,\u00a0\r\n\u6728\u6f0f\u308c\u65e5[komorebi] het gefilterde zonlicht dat speelt door het bladerdek van een boom\u00a0\r\n\r\nOp het eind van deze kleine fenomenologie van het licht, voegde ze nog een ander Japans woord\u00a0\u9593 [ma] toe. Ma is zowel ruimte als tijd. Het betekent in feite interval, een afstand of een periode. Met ander woorden een relatie. Als dochter van een Japanse moeder en een Belgische vader belichaamt Michiko\u00a0bij wijze van spreken\u9593\u00a0[ma]. Ze leeft \u2018tussen\u2019 twee culturen, tussen twee ruimtes en tijden.\r\n\r\nZonder te willen psychologiseren, lijkt het alsof\u00a0Michiko\u00a0dit bewustzijn van de meervoudigheid van tijd en ruimte, en vooral de ongrijpbaarheid van tijd wil vangen in beelden.\u00a0\r\nDie vliedende tijd en ruimte is voor haar zichtbaar en tastbaar in het permanent veranderen van het licht.\r\n\r\nIn een aantal werken legt ze zich toe op de simultane\u00efteit van het licht in Tokyo en Brussel. Doorgaans is dat heel verschillend, maar twee keer per jaar, valt de zonsopgang in Brussel en de zonsondergang in Tokyo verrassend samen.\r\nIn haar ander werk draait het vaak om het \u2018vangen van het licht\u2019 en het ogenblik waarin een waarneming in een flits weer is verdwenen.\r\n\r\nMichiko\u00a0Van de Velde gebruikt verschillende technieken.\u00a0\r\nZe tekent haar observaties: lichtvlekken met potlood op papier of met een droge naald rechtstreeks op metalen graveerplaten.\r\nIn situ tekent en schildert ze, of \u2018strooit\u2019 natuurlijke, reflecterende mica deeltjes om de invallende zonnevlekken te \u2018vangen\u2019.\u00a0\r\nZe schildert gefotografeerde zichten vanuit rijdende treinen, inclusief het spel van lichtreflecties en spiegelingen van ramen in ramen.\u00a0\r\nMet video legde ze op straat het kleurige, flikkerende licht vast van reclameborden afstraalt\u00a0op mistsluiers. Maar ze \u00ab\u00a0documenteerde\u00a0\u00bb ook zichzelf, met name wanneer ze met vrije hand ronde lichtvlekken probeert te tekenen die door het gebladerte van een boom vallen (\u6728\u6f0f\u308c\u65e5[komorebi]). In die video valt op hoe snel die lichtvlekken over het witte blad schuiven door de rotatie van de aarde. Het is quasi onmogelijk om de vlek in zijn geheel te tekenen omdat tussen de aanzet en het sluiten van de lijntekening, de vlek al is opgeschoven.\r\n\r\nDat \u201cvluchtige\u2019 licht en de vluchtigheid der dingen komt samen in het woord\u00a0\u6728\u6f0f\u308c\u65e5[komorebi] waarbij de kanji\u00a0\u6f0f[mo] onder meer verwijst naar een lek \u00e9n vlucht.\u00a0\r\nMisschien moeten we naar\u00a0Michiko\u00a0Van de\u00a0Velde werk kijken, als een heruitgave van \u2018Kunst der Fuge\u2019. Want net als de in muzikale fuga\u2019s van J.S. Bach transformeert ze de vluchtigheid en de ongrijpbaarheid van de tijd in levenskunst.\u00a0\r\n\r\nKoen Van Synghel, kunst criticus","performers":"Michiko Van de Velde (\u00b01994, Brasschaat (B)) Belgo-Japanese kunstenares, leeft en werkt in Brussel.","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.micheleschoonjansgallery.be","email":"info@micheleschoonjansgallery.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":"+32 478 71 62 96","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/nl\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.551153"},"en":{"name":"Michiko Van de Velde - Timing","shortdescr":"In a number of works, she focuses on the simultaneity of the sunlight in Tokyo and Brussels. They are typically very different, but surprisingly, the sunrise in Brussels and sunset in Tokyo coincide twice a year. Other work often revolves around 'catching the light' and the moment when a sighting disappears again in a flash.","longdescr":"\u201cComment parle-t-on de la lumi\u00e8re (au Japon)?\u201d\r\n\u201cQuelle lumi\u00e8re? Celle de quand?\u201d\r\n(an extract from the book\u00a0 \u201c Lumi\u00e8res \u5149\u00a0\u201c\u00a0, self-publishing, 2017)\r\nLight?\u00a0\r\nSpace?\u00a0\r\nTime?\u00a0\r\n\r\nWhat are we talking about while observing Michiko Van de Velde's work?\r\nAnd in what language should we speak?\u00a0\r\nIn 2017, she created \u201cLumi\u00e8res\u201d, a booklet in which she collected dozens of Japanese words referencing the different aspects of light, like for example:\r\n\u63a1\u5149[saik\u014d] Letting the outside light into your home. \r\n\u8584\u65e5[usubi] Weak, soft, faint light, like a grey shroud or Brussels skies.\r\n\u4e5d\u5341\u6625\u5149\u00a0[kujun\u014d\u00a0shunk\u014d] Peaceful spring light that lasts 90 days, from March to June.\r\n\u6708\u767d[tsuki shiro] As the moon ri ses, the eastern sky becomes brighter, whiter.\r\n\u6728\u6f0f\u308c\u65e5[komorebi] Sunlight filters through the trees: a play of light in the leaves.\r\n\r\nAt the end of this little phenomenology of light, she added another Japanese word: \u9593 [ma]. Ma is both space and time. It basically means interval, a distance or a period of time. In other words, a relationship. Daughter of a Japanese mother and a Belgian father, Michiko incarnates, so to speak\u9593\u00a0[ma]. She lives 'between' two cultures, between two spaces and times.\r\n\r\nHowever, without going too deep into psychology, Michiko seems to want to capture the awareness of this plurality of time and space, and especially the elusiveness of time, in images.\u00a0For her, the fleeting time and space is visible and tangible in the permanently changing light.\r\n\r\nIn a number of works, she focuses on the simultaneity of the sunlight in Tokyo and Brussels. They are typically very different, but surprisingly, the sunrise in Brussels and sunset in Tokyo coincide twice a year. Other work often revolves around 'catching the light' and the moment when a sighting disappears again in a flash.\r\n\r\nMichiko Van de Velde uses a variety of techniques.\u00a0\r\nShe draws what she sees: light spots with pencil on paper or directly engraving onto metal plates. \r\nIn situ, she draws, paints, or 'scatters' reflective natural mica flakes to 'catch\u2019 momentary sunlight.\u00a0\r\nShe paints photographed views from moving trains, including the play of light reflections within the windows.\u00a0\r\n\r\nWith moving images, she captured the colourful fog veils lit by an advertising billboard in the Brussels city center. She also \"documented\" herself, when she used freehand to draw circular spots of sunlight falling through the foliage of a tree (\u6728\u6f0f\u308c\u65e5[komorebi]). In that moving image, you might notice how quickly the earth is spinning by looking at the movement of the sunlight spots sliding on the paper. The shadows move so quickly that it is almost impossible to draw the whole circular sunlight shape: the beginning and ending of this drawing aren\u2019t in the same place. \r\n\r\nThat \"fleeting\" light and the volatility of things comes together in the word \u6728\u6f0f\u308c\u65e5[komorebi] where\u2028the kanji \u6f0f[mo] refers, among other things, to a leak as well as flight\/escape.\u00a0Perhaps we should look at Michiko Van de Velde's work as a reappropriation of 'Kunst der Fuge'. As in the in musical fugues by J.S. Bach, she transforms the volatility and elusiveness of time into the art of living.\u00a0\r\n\u00a0\r\nKoen Van Synghel, art critic","performers":"Michiko Van de Velde (\u00b01994, Braaschaat (B), Belgo-Japanese artist, lives and works in Brussels.","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.micheleschoonjansgallery.be","email":"info@micheleschoonjansgallery.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":"+32 478 71 62 96","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/en\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.551153"},"de":{"name":"Michiko Van de Velde - Timing","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.micheleschoonjansgallery.be","email":"info@micheleschoonjansgallery.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":"+32 478 71 62 96","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/de\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.551153"},"it":{"name":"Michiko Van de Velde - Timing","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.micheleschoonjansgallery.be","email":"info@micheleschoonjansgallery.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":"+32 478 71 62 96","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/it\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.551153"},"sp":{"name":"Michiko Van de Velde - Timing","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.micheleschoonjansgallery.be","email":"info@micheleschoonjansgallery.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":"+32 478 71 62 96","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/sp\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.551153"},"pt":{"name":"Michiko Van de Velde - Timing","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.micheleschoonjansgallery.be","email":"info@micheleschoonjansgallery.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":"+32 478 71 62 96","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/pt\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.551153"},"cn":{"name":"Michiko Van de Velde - Timing","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.micheleschoonjansgallery.be","email":"info@micheleschoonjansgallery.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":"+32 478 71 62 96","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/cn\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.551153"}},"place":{"id":275036,"translations":{"fr":{"name":"Mich\u00e8le Schoonjans Gallery","address_street_name":"Chauss\u00e9e de Waterloo","address_street_number":"690","address_street_box":"Rivoli #25","email":"info@micheleschoonjansgallery.be","website":"http:\/\/www.micheleschoonjansgallery.be","phone_contact":"+32 478 71 62 96","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1180","address_city":"Uccle","address_line1":"Chauss\u00e9e de Waterloo, 690\/Rivoli #25","address_line2":"1180 Uccle","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"nl":{"name":"Mich\u00e8le Schoonjans Gallery","address_street_name":"Waterloosesteenweg","address_street_number":"690","address_street_box":"Rivoli #25","email":"info@micheleschoonjansgal